title: A rented 4-vCPU, 8 GB Linux machine is enough to develop skg, at about €30 a month; missions wait on the model, not on the tests.
pid: 71fea003-732f-4c14-ac71-b98bc05de105
body: |2-
  Measured 2026-11-15 on this laptop, with four of its slower cores
  standing in for a rented machine's four vCPUs. Nothing here was run
  on a rented machine, so the speeds there are an estimate, likely
  somewhat slower.
  The biggest load is a debug build linking the test binaries (3.4 GiB
  at four jobs), beside the servers and Claude's own processes (about
  4 GB together). The whole test suite uses less than one core: it is
  mostly waiting. And in the last five days the model's own time was
  three quarters of all working time, the tests about a tenth.
